ly more than he's moving  around right now  well and here's the other side of it as  well um  he may not be comfortable in these other  spots right i mean receivers aren't  always comfortable in the x the y and  the z sometimes you know i go to the  left side i want the left side i don't  want the right side i don't want to be  in the slot this is this is the spot  that i'm the most comfortable in getting  the play started now we see him on the  outside on either side but it may just  be he's not as comfortable operating out  of the slot chris yeah maybe but i think  he's he'll be comfortable anywhere once  he goes oh the play doh designs for me  and it's kind of creative and it's going  to give me some space or create a  one-on-one you know that's where i just  don't see like where's odell beckham jr  over the middle why don't we ever see  deep crosses to odell beckham jr and  things like that and that comes a lot of  times with like okay here's two  receivers and here's odell beckham jr  getting in the bunch and these two  receivers go vertical and do something  and he kind of plays off behind him and  the defense doesn't know like oh is he  going to go right or is he going to go  left i don't know what he's going to do  and then he breaks it off for a deep  cross or you know something of that  nature is really what i'm just trying to  say and uh i know freddie kitchens has  got his hands full baker mayfield's  still learning on the fly but i do think  ultimately that's the thing that i would  like to change about them and odell  right now  and that's really the bottom line it's  not odell beckham jr all of a sudden not  being one of the best receivers in the  nfl right the browns haven't figured out  how to properly use him they haven't  designed the plays they haven't used the  creativity that is available to them i  don't know what they expected would  happen i think they just thought it  would be automatic and it would be  simple it would be easy and sometimes